     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\">I would like to display some text and be able to get the positions\r\nof the highlighted area (if a user has highlighted some part of the text).<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I’m think of an api like this: <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">html_txt </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">“</span><span style=\"color:#606\">My</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> little text</span><span style=\"color:#660\">”</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Render_selectable</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">html_text</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">It would be queryable:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Suppose a user has highlighted the word “little”<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"></p><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#606\">Input$selectable</span></div></code></div><p></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">would return </p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"></p><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">9</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><p></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I plan to base myself on this little javascript example:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><a href=\"http://jsfiddle.net/L9bvU/1/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://jsfiddle.net/L9bvU/1/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792396175299000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2r0STwNqapHRMkRas_g5i1\">http://jsfiddle.net/L9bvU/1/</a><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">What’s not clear to me is whether this fits the htmlwidgets\r\nframework, since I couldn’t find examples with communication from the gui back\r\nto the backend.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Maybe it should be a custom input binding (<a href=\"http://shiny.rstudio.com/articles/building-inputs.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shiny.rstudio.com/articles/building-inputs.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792396175299000&amp;usg=AOvVaw08Gb985_yy0Nu4XLFFBx9d\">http://shiny.rstudio.com/articles/building-inputs.html</a>),\r\nbut reactivity is not a requirement here.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Any advice ?<u></u><u></u></p></div>"
    ]
